#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""posts_show extraction with INCREMENTAL dedup (results3-local driver).

ARCHIVED 2026-09-10: this is the 2026-08-19 version, superseded by the
upgraded _extract_posts_show_streaming.py (E1 AssocFoldingTransformer, E11
RED check, broadened-bind notes, tri-state subsumption tally). Kept verbatim
so the upgrade is diffable. DO NOT RUN — it is the version with the E11 blind
spot.

Why this exists: `queries_from_runs.dump.build_endpoint_file` accumulates
every TransformedQuery from every run before deduping (689,601 objects for
posts_show's 18,688 dumps) — that list blew the 4.5G MemoryMax cgroup cap on
the 2026-08-19 re-run (and is the same load pattern behind the 2026-08-18
kernel OOM kills). This driver replicates build_endpoint_file exactly, but
dedups by SQL string as it streams, so memory stays at the per-dump scale.
Output (.sql file + summary JSON) is byte-identical in content to dump.py's:
dedup keeps the FIRST TransformedQuery per SQL string in both versions, and
flag/placeholder/skipped-PC counters are accumulated pre-dedup in both.
src/ is untouched (source-code discipline).

KEY DIFFERENCES from the upgrade, i.e. WHY it was superseded:
  * `RunTransformer`, not `AssocFoldingTransformer` — every `assoc_*` bind
    stays an unresolved placeholder (E1).
  * `errors` is collected and never checked: an unparseable note silently
    deletes a statement the app really issues (E11).
  * `can_subsume` does not exclude `broadened-*` flags.
  * no POLICY_HEADER, no provenance block.
  * `subsume_ran` is a bool, so "never attempted" reads as "attempted and
    failed".
"""
